... Just to answer to the previous post (the post has been "locked"), "220" is supported. I have this radio and I use it for 220 Mhz. But 220 is only used in North America and is forbidden in Europe for amateur bands.<br><br>The web site is not well done, some pages says it is supported, other pages hide it, but I confirm that the 220 is supported. See picture 1 (1/5) here : <a href="https://www.zastone.com/product/showproduct.php?id=117&amp;lang=en" class="postlink">https://www.zastone.com/product/showpro ... 17&amp;lang=en</a><br><br>Except some Motorola's, this is one of the rare handheld radio supporting DMR in 220.<br><br>As I am not a programmer, so I will let this radio "as is".<br><br>Thanks for answering.<br><br>Yves,<br>ve2ymm.com<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7035">ve2ymm</a> — Tue Oct 15, 2024 5:12 pm</p><hr />
